   155	## 2. Bundle format
   156	
   157	### 2.1 Members
   158	
   159	A V1 bundle carries these twelve members. Nothing is taken from outside the bundle except the trust configuration
   160	(section 5). The last column is the container member that carries each one (section 15.1). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G14,
   161	G17]
   162	
   163	| # | Member | Source | Container member |
   164	|---|---|---|---|
   165	| 1 | Unsigned profile label (read first, for dispatch) | [ENC §8:742-743] | top-level `profile` |
   166	| 2 | The receipt tuple `(F_kms, S_kms, F_gpg, S_gpg)`, or `A_sig`, which encodes it | [ENC §5.3:493-497] | `a_sig` only (one tuple route) |
   167	| 3 | The manifest frame `F_manifest` and each key's possession signature over it | [ENC §4:362-369; A9:311-312] | `manifest`, `possession` |
   168	| 4 | The two public keys, checked against the manifest fingerprints | [ENC §5.3:509] | `keys` |
   169	| 5 | The DNSSEC snapshot (envelope per ENC §6) and its own OTS proof | [ENC §6:536-542; DD:94] | `dns` |
   170	| 6 | The git key-assertion evidence: raw signed commit object, the tree objects on the path, the blob, and the OTS proof stamped on the commit id | [ENC §7.2:706-710; A9:282-284] | `git` |
   171	| 7 | The receipt's OTS proof and the anchor transaction id | [SPEC R-3.42:679-682] | `receipt_anchor` |
   172	| 8 | Bitcoin block headers needed by the proof, each of which must be in the pinned set | [A9:150; DD:99] | `headers` (one pool) |
   173	| 9 | The verification specification bytes (content-addressed) | [A9:152-153; ENC §3.2:281] | `spec` |
   174	| 10 | The conformance vector bytes (content-addressed) | [A9:152-153; ENC §3.2:281] | `vectors` |
   175	| 11 | The plain-language purpose preamble, bound by hash in the signed bytes | [A9:153; ENC §3.2:281] | `preamble` |
   176	| 12 | The dependency manifest (section 9) | [A9:153-154] | `dependency_manifest` |
   177	| — | Observed anchor delay and issue-time policy version (R-3.46), optional diagnostics | [SPEC R-3.46:698-700] | `issuer_record` |
   178	
   179	- Members 9, 10 and 11 are bound by SHA-256 of their raw bytes, inside the signed common bytes. They are never signed
   180	  or anchored on their own. [ENC §0:71-72; ENC §3.2:281]
   181	- The OTS proof, txid, headers and confirmation evidence are outside `A_sig`. [ENC §5:402-405]
   182	- The txid sits in the bundle outside the signed bytes. [SPEC R-3.43:685-687]
   183	- **Container.** One canonical JCS JSON text, no JSON numbers, top level exactly
   184	  `{"layers":[L],"profile":"tessera-v1-strict"}`, with the closed layer schema of section 15.1. ~~A required member
   185	  that is absent, at any nesting level, gives `UNVERIFIABLE / MEMBER_MISSING:<path>`; this rule precedes the generic
   186	  schema rule.~~ *(Withdrawn 2026-10-14, r2-F03: it contradicted the `object_format` and `issuer_record`
   187	  exceptions and left a null parent ambiguous.)* **Absence and presence** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F03]: "A missing
   188	  required evidence member contributes UNVERIFIABLE/MEMBER_MISSING:<path>, except git.object_format, which
   189	  contributes GIT_OBJECT_FORMAT_MISSING. A present parent of the wrong type contributes CONTAINER_SCHEMA; do not
   190	  synthesize missing descendants beneath it. Absence of issuer_record is allowed; any defect in a present
   191	  issuer_record, including absent internal fields, contributes INVALID/CONTAINER_SCHEMA. Absence and schema failures
   192	  are collected independently; INVALID still dominates. Nested absence is inspected only beneath correctly typed
   193	  parents." `<path>` is the layer-relative dotted schema path (`git`, `git.ots`, `keys.gpg`; array members by
   194	  numeric index); several missing paths are compared in JCS key order with array indices numeric. A present
   195	  `git.object_format` that is a JSON string other than `"sha1"` is A9.5's unsupported value (`UNVERIFIABLE /
   196	  GIT_OBJECT_FORMAT`); a present non-string value, `null` included, is a schema failure (`INVALID /
   197	  CONTAINER_SCHEMA`), not absence (**owner choice**, fail-closed; the honest issuer emits `"sha1"`). A present
   198	  nonconforming member or an unnamed member gives `INVALID / CONTAINER_SCHEMA`. The receipt
   199	  tuple is taken only by decoding `a_sig`. Re-indenting a container makes it `INVALID / JSON_NONCANONICAL`
   200	  (a visible custody restriction: keep the bytes, do not reformat). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G14, G17] *(Was:
   201	  "`OPEN (other):` the container and transport encoding, member names and member order", 2026-10-13.)*
   202	- **Observed delay and policy version** are carried in the optional `issuer_record` member: unsigned diagnostics.
   203	  Absence never affects the verdict; a present record is schema-checked (`INVALID / CONTAINER_SCHEMA`); its values
   204	  never alter verification parameters and are not authenticated observations. The honest issuer always emits it.
   205	  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G33] *(Was: "`OPEN (other):` where the observed anchor delay and the issue-time policy version
   206	  are recorded", 2026-10-13.)*
