   844	
   845	### 7.1 The T rule
   846	
   847	- T is the time of the verified attestation at the **lowest block height** in the presented OTS proof; both T and
   848	  its confirmations come from that attestation. It is presentation-sensitive: a different presentation of the same
   849	  receipt can select a different T. [A9 C5 as revised 2026-10-14; DD:56, 98-99; OWNER 2026-10-14, G03] *Dated
   850	  correction 2026-10-14: this bullet previously read "T is the time of the earliest verified attestation", A9's
   851	  earlier wording. "Earliest" means chain order, not least nTime: header times are not monotone, and the two
   852	  selection rules can give different verdicts on the same proof.*
   853	- No lower bound and no priority. Header times are chain-time proxies. [A9:138]
   854	- The three conjuncts at k = 6 (`DepthK = k − 1 = 5`): `declared − ε ≤ anchor_time`; `anchor_time ≤ declared + δ`;
   855	  `confirmed_at ≤ declared + δ`. All three are evaluated together. [SPEC R-4.41:985; SPEC R-5.19:1352; SPEC
   856	  V33-V36:1342-1346; A9:99]
   857	- A real proof carries several attestations hours apart and nothing in the proof names T (M3). [FT:20; DD:98]
   858	- **T ≡ `anchor_time`.** For the receipt proof, T = `anchor_time` = nTime(h*), where h* is the lowest qualifying
   859	  height. The same value feeds conjuncts 1 and 2, the C4 window rule and the reported T. Two qualifying attestations
   860	  at the same height give the same T. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G03] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` one sentence stating whether
   861	  T is the `anchor_time` of the three conjuncts", 2026-10-13.)*
   862	- **`confirmed_at`** = nTime(h* + 5): the including block plus five successors, k = 6 (SPEC R-3.45, R-4.42). A
   863	  failure gives `INVALID`: `TIME_BEFORE_DECLARED_EPSILON`, `TIME_AFTER_DECLARED_DELTA` or `CONFIRMATION_LATE`.
   864	  Nonmonotone header times can give `confirmed_at` < T; that is not a failure, and there is no monotonicity check.
   865	  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G04]
   866	- **Qualifying ("verified") attestation.** A Bitcoin attestation at height h qualifies if and only if (a) the
   867	  bundled header at h exists and its merkle root equals the attestation message; (b) headers h … h+5 are all
   868	  bundled; (c) each equals its pin, `hex(reverse(SHA256d(header))) = pin[height]`; (d) for i = h+1 … h+5,
   869	  `header_i.prev = SHA256d(header_{i−1})`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` what 'verified' means
   870	  for an attestation", 2026-10-13.)*
   871	- **Selection.** Attestation selection is existential over qualifying branches. A syntactically valid Bitcoin
   872	  attestation without a complete h..h+5 segment is nonqualifying, not a required failed check. It supplies no time or
   873	  trust fact. All supplied headers, including unused ones, are independently checked against pins (section 7.2).
   874	  The selected anchor, rather than every unverified attestation, is the referent of "anchors beyond the newest pin"
   875	  (A9 C6 as revised 2026-10-14). [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05]
   876	- **Proof outcomes.** A pinned bundled header at h whose merkle root ≠ the attestation message: `INVALID /
   877	  OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH` (a contradicted branch fails the proof). No qualifying attestation: `UNVERIFIABLE /
   878	  HEADERS_MISSING` if any Bitcoin attestation is present, `UNVERIFIABLE / ANCHOR_PENDING_ONLY` if only pending ones;
   879	  the snapshot uses `SNAPSHOT_NOT_ANCHORED` and git `GIT_NOT_ANCHORED`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G05]
   880	- **Time arithmetic.** Times are integer seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z without leap seconds; nTime is the
   881	  header's uint32; RFC 3339 fields convert by days-from-civil (proleptic Gregorian); comparisons are inclusive.
   882	  [OWNER 2026-10-14, G03]
