   915	### 7.3 The DNSSEC snapshot rule
   916	
   917	- The issuer anchors the DNSSEC snapshot with its own OTS proof. The envelope is ENC §6 under the tag
   918	  `tessera-v1/dnssec-snapshot`. [DD:94; ENC §6:536-542]
   919	- The verifier checks that the snapshot's anchored time lies inside every RRSIG window in the chain and within
   920	  [declared − ε, declared + δ]. The issuer re-captures before shipping if it does not. [DD:94] This is an owner
   921	  decision carried in, not routed. [A9:99-101]
   922	  - "declared" is the receipt's signed `declared_issue_time`, not the snapshot's capture time. Capture-to-anchor
   923	    latency is a separate observation, not this predicate. (`docs/reviews/v1-profile/` F6, accepted 2026-10-13.)
   924	  - "every RRSIG window in the chain" means the one witness signature selected to authenticate each required RRset,
   925	    not every signature offered: an extra expired or invalid signature beside a valid one neither fails the RRset
   926	    nor narrows the joint window. The instrument's selection order is (key tag, inception, expiration, signature
   927	    bytes), first that validates. (`docs/reviews/v1-profile/` F5, accepted 2026-10-13.) Exception: an RRSIG
   928	    with fewer Labels than its owner fails the body restriction wherever it appears (section 6.1).
   929	    [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F07]
   930	  - **Frozen witness rule.** The selected witness is the **first eligible validating** candidate in (key tag,
   931	    inception, expiration, signature bytes, canonical RRSIG RDATA, canonical key RDATA) order. For the root, reliance
   932	    eligibility precedes selection. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G35] *(Previously described only as the instrument's order.)*
   933	  - Conjunct 3 (`confirmed_at` of the snapshot ≤ declared + δ) is a new owner acceptance restriction, fail-closed. A
   934	    failure of any conjunct gives `INVALID / SNAPSHOT_TIME`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G06]
   935	- The chain is evaluated at the snapshot's anchored time, not at T of the receipt. [A9:137]
   936	- Why: the joint RRSIG window measured 1.6 days, shorter than δ (M8). [DD:93]
   937	- **Snapshot body.** A fixed-order sequence of uncompressed RFC 1035 wire RRs in RFC 4034 §6.2 canonical form,
   938	  section 15.3. Framing violations are `INVALID / SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`; a syntactically complete body lacking a required
   939	  RRset or its witness RRSIG is `UNVERIFIABLE / DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING` (root: `NO_TRUSTED_KSK_USABLE`). The conversion
   940	  from resolver messages happens before stamping and changes S, so each snapshot needs a fresh stamp; earlier
   941	  stamped JSON snapshots cannot be reused. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G19] *(Was: "`OPEN (step 8):` the snapshot body
   942	  format", 2026-10-13.)*
