   948	  second t with t ≡ v (mod 2^32) and |t − T_snap| < 2^31 (RFC 4034 §3.1.5, RFC 1982). If v − T_snap ≡ 2^31 (mod 2^32)
   949	  the candidate fails with `RRSIG_TIME_AMBIGUOUS`; if resolved inception > expiration it fails with
   950	  `RRSIG_INTERVAL_REVERSED`; inception = expiration is allowed. These are candidate failures under the existential
   951	  rule, ranked with `RRSIG_NOT_VALID_AT_EVAL_TIME`. The witness check is inception ≤ T_snap ≤ expiration, never "now",
   952	  including in 2106. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G27]
