   954	### 7.4 The UTC assessment [OWNER 2026-10-19, A10.1.1]
   955	
   956	A10.1.1 (AUTHOR ADOPTED 2026-10-18, BROADEN; A10 rows 20–24) adds one reported assessment and one named assumption.
   957	Nothing in this subsection changes T, a verdict, a reason code, the check order or the stable field set.
   958	
   959	- **Assumption A-UTC** (`assumption_id` `"A-UTC-7200-6"`). At least one of the six blocks h* … h*+5 has a header
   960	  time no more than 7200 s before it was actually mined: `nTime(j) ≥ r(j) − 7200 s` for some j in [h*, h*+5], where
   961	  r(j) is the real (UTC) time block j was first produced. It is an assumption of the UTC assessment only, not a
   962	  Bitcoin consensus rule; **the verifier does not check it** and no bundle carries evidence of it. It is sufficient,
   963	  not minimal. [A10:280-285]
   964	- **Constants.** Δ = 7200 s and m = 6 are frozen catalog constants (section 1), not trust-configuration data, and
   965	  are not shown to be optimal. m = 6 is the same six-header segment h* … h*+5 that section 7.1 already requires and
   966	  pins (k = 6), so U needs no new input. [A10:284-285; A10 row 22; A10:343-344] *Instrument note: the TEST catalog
   967	  wire object (section 3.5; `prototype/differential/ADAPTER.md` T2) does not yet carry Δ and m; both instruments
   968	  compile them in. Adding them to the frozen catalog object is owner work before the freeze.*
   969	- **h\*** is the receipt proof's selected inclusion height (section 7.1, A10.5); it counts as confirmation one, so
   970	  h*+5 is confirmation six. [A10:277-278]
   971	- **Definition.** `U_seconds = 7200 + max(uint64(nTime(h*)), uint64(nTime(h*+1)), …, uint64(nTime(h*+5)))`, the
   972	  maximum over the receipt proof's selected h* and its six qualified headers (section 7.1 items (a)–(d)). Header
   973	  times need not be monotone: the maximum is taken over all six, not nTime(h*+5) and not T. Each nTime is the
   974	  header's unsigned 32-bit little-endian field (section 7.1 "Time arithmetic"), widened to 64 bits **before** the
   975	  addition; the sum is never reduced modulo 2^32. [A10:287-293; A10:307-311]
   976	- **Encoding.** `utc_upper_bound` is the RFC 3339 UTC string of U_seconds in the form used for T
   977	  (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`, days-from-civil, no leap seconds). For max nTime = 4294967295, U = 4294974495 =
   978	  `2106-02-07T08:28:15Z`, not a 1970 time. [A10:309-311]
   979	- **Null rule.** `utc_upper_bound` is `null` exactly when T is `null` (section 3.4), including every D1–D4
   980	  dispatch-terminal outcome; otherwise it is computed from the same selected h* that gives T. The object
   981	  `utc_assessment`, with `assumption_id`, is present on every report reached after dispatch. [A10:300-302]
   982	- **No verdict effect.** U never enters a verdict, reason code, stable field, the shipping predicate or S; a value
   983	  is reported whatever the verdict, and with `INVALID` or `UNVERIFIABLE` it does not establish a valid service
   984	  receipt or valid service signatures. [A10:302-305; A10:347-348; A10 row 21]
   985	- **Clock.** Verification does not consult the current clock; the arithmetic covers preserved headers. Timestamp
   986	  representation for Bitcoin blocks produced after the 2106 rollover of the 32-bit field is a Bitcoin protocol
   987	  matter outside V1. Section 7.3's serial-time unwrapping applies to DNSSEC RRSIG fields only, never to nTime.
   988	  [A10:307-313; A10 row 24]
   989	- **Claim, as registered** (A10:289-293): under A-UTC, the bytes and both signatures existed before U, in UTC. A2.1's
   990	  refusal to bound the observation lag B − C is unchanged; guarantee 2 keeps its chain-time meaning (A10 row 23).
   991	  A-UTC is false exactly when every one of the six blocks has a header time more than 7200 s before its production;
   992	  then the conditional UTC guarantee is unavailable, though the computed value need not itself be false (A10 row
   993	  24).
