  1166	## 10. Number rule
  1167	
  1168	Accept a number exactly when RFC 8785's canonical serialization preserves its value. Reject otherwise. The three
  1169	conditions (not negative zero, finite after round-half-even, exact decimal value of `ES(d)` equals the literal) and
  1170	the accepted and rejected examples are in ENC §1.2. [A9:438-443; ENC §1.2:118-148; ENC D-1:752-755] Proof:
  1171	`formal/p8/PROOF.md` Lemma 3. Vectors: `formal/p8/vectors/`.
  1172	
  1173	This replaces the literal "exactly representable as an IEEE 754 double" rule for this profile only. [A9:405-406;
  1174	A9:440-443] The stale "needs an author sentence" remarks in ENC (ENC:147-148, D-1) and PROOF §6 are superseded by
  1175	A9.8. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G38; the ENC and PROOF wording edits are done, OWNER 2026-10-19]
  1176	
  1177	**`ES` recipe.** `ES(d)` is ECMA-262 NumberToString (7.1.12.1, Note 2) of the 10th edition (June 2019), the edition RFC 8785 cites
  1178	(edition, section and digest in the dependency manifest; later editions rename it Number::toString with the same
  1179	output) [OWNER 2026-10-19, item 15; source formal/dependency-sources/MANIFEST.md]. If d is +0 or −0: `"0"`. If d < 0: `"-"` ‖ ES(−d). Otherwise let n, k, s be integers with
  1180	k ≥ 1, 10^(k−1) ≤ s < 10^k, s × 10^(n−k) = d as a double, and k as small as possible; if several s qualify, choose
  1181	the one for which s × 10^(n−k) is closest in value to d, and if two are equally close, the even one. Then: if
  1182	k ≤ n ≤ 21, the k digits followed by n−k zeros; if 0 < n ≤ 21, the first n digits, `.`, the remaining k−n digits;
  1183	if −6 < n ≤ 0, `0.`, −n zeros, the digits; otherwise the first digit, then `.` and the remaining digits if k > 1,
  1184	then `e`, `+` or `-`, and abs(n−1) in decimal. Any formatter must reproduce N-01…N-22 and C-N01…C-N22; Python's
  1185	`repr` is not ES. Unicode tables must be 16.0.0, identified by the UCD file digests in the dependency manifest; a
  1186	runtime may use bundled pinned tables, and one whose tables do not match refuses to run (no verdict).
