  1546	### 15.3 DNSSEC snapshot body [OWNER 2026-10-14, G19, G24, G30]
  1547	
  1548	A concatenation of RRs, each in RFC 1035 §3.2.1 wire format, uncompressed, in RFC 4034 §6.2 canonical form (owner
  1549	name and every domain-name field inside RDATA, including the RRSIG signer name, lowercase and uncompressed).
  1550	1. **Groups, in order:** the root DNSKEY group; then for each zone z below the root down to the TXT's signer zone, a
  1551	   DS group at z and a DNSKEY group at z; last the TXT group at `_tessera-v1.<D>`. A group is a maximal run of RRs
  1552	   with the same owner, CLASS IN, and TYPE t (the RRset) or TYPE RRSIG with Type Covered t (its witnesses). The RRset
  1553	   comes first, in RFC 4034 §6.3 canonical RDATA order without duplicates, then zero or more RRSIGs in (key tag,
  1554	   inception, expiration, signature bytes) order. Each z is a proper descendant of the previous zone. Signer names:
  1555	   the parent for DS, z for DNSKEY, the root for the root group, the last z for TXT.
  1556	   - **Serialization ties and duplicates** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F07]. Canonical RRSIG RDATA is the final body
  1557	     serialization sort key: RRSIGs sort by (key tag, inception, expiration, signature bytes, canonical RRSIG
  1558	     RDATA). A duplicate is an RR identical in owner, class, type and RDATA (`SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`); TTL consistency
  1559	     within an RRset is checked separately (point 2).
  1560	   - **Raw time fields in sort keys.** Inception and expiration in these sort keys, and in the G35 candidate tuple
  1561	     (section 7.3), are the raw 32-bit unsigned RRSIG field values compared numerically (equivalently, as
  1562	     big-endian bytes), not the absolute times resolved by section 7.3's serial arithmetic; the two orders differ
  1563	     only across the 2^32 wrap. [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from diff-1, EA-13]
  1564	   - **Too-short RRSIG.** An RRSIG whose RDATA (within a consistent RDLENGTH) is too short for RFC 4034 §3.1's
  1565	     fixed fields and signer name is attributed to the group of the immediately preceding RRs at the same owner,
  1566	     not treated as a framing failure, and is malformed supported RRSIG RDATA: `INVALID / DNSSEC_FORMAT`
  1567	     (section 6.1). [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from diff-1, A06]
  1568	   - **Chain skeleton, recovery grammar** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F06]. The root is the initial zone. The ordered zone
  1569	     skeleton is constructed from the supplied DS and DNSKEY owners and the RRSIG signer names: each names a zone,
  1570	     and the zones, ordered by descent, must form one chain from the root. Omitted DS, DNSKEY, root DNSKEY or TXT
  1571	     groups are admitted as missing evidence (`UNVERIFIABLE / DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING`; root:
  1572	     `NO_TRUSTED_KSK_USABLE`); omission alone is never a format failure. Direct signing of the TXT by the root, or
  1573	     by any ancestor zone in the skeleton, is permitted (section 6.1 retains ancestor signing authority); "the last
  1574	     z" is the TXT RRSIG's signer zone, which is the root when no below-root zone is supplied. Conflicting supplied
  1575	     transitions or signer names (names not forming one descent chain, a DS group not signed by its parent zone in
  1576	     the skeleton, a DNSKEY group not signed by its own zone, a group after the TXT group) are `INVALID /
  1577	     SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`. A supplied final TXT owner is checked by ENC §7's `DNS_OWNER`, even when wrong; its existence
  1578	     does not itself constitute an "outside-chain" framing failure. *(Dated correction 2026-10-14: the grammar did
  1579	     not say whether a skipped zone was omission or inconsistency, and "the last z" was undefined for a TXT signed
  1580	     by the root.)*
  1581	2. **Fields.** CLASS IN. TTL equal within an RRset and otherwise uninterpreted; validation uses the RRSIG's Original
  1582	   TTL.
  1583	3. **Framing versus completeness.** A truncated RR encoding, forbidden RR type, duplicate RR, inconsistent
  1584	   owner/type within a group, or misordered supplied group is `INVALID / SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`. Among RDATA defects,
  1585	   RR boundary/RDLENGTH truncation and any domain-name field inside RDATA that is not in the canonical form above (an
  1586	   uppercase ASCII letter or a compression pointer, including in the RRSIG signer name) are `INVALID /
  1587	   SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`, whatever other witnesses the body carries; TXT's internal character-string parsing uses ENC's
  1588	   `DNS_RDATA` / `DNS_STRINGS`, and other malformed supported DNSKEY/RRSIG RDATA is `DNSSEC_FORMAT` (section 6.1).
  1589	   [OWNER 2026-10-14, diff-1 F-1: the earlier wording let a non-canonical RRSIG beside a valid witness reach
  1590	   `VALID_STRICT` in one implementation and `INVALID` in another; fail-closed chosen.]
  1591	   A defect in an RR's owner-name wire encoding is `SNAPSHOT_FORMAT`; a defect of the RRSIG signer-name field
  1592	   other than the non-canonical forms just named (which are `SNAPSHOT_FORMAT` under diff-1 F-1) and other than a
  1593	   recovery-grammar conflict is malformed supported RRSIG RDATA, `DNSSEC_FORMAT`. [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from
  1594	   diff-1, A12]
  1595	   [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F06, r2-F05] A syntactically complete
  1596	   sequence lacking a required RRset or its witness RRSIG is `UNVERIFIABLE / DNS_EVIDENCE_MISSING` (root:
  1597	   `NO_TRUSTED_KSK_USABLE`). Missing groups alone are not order violations. Forbidden: any type other than DNSKEY, DS,
  1598	   TXT and RRSIG, and any RR at a name outside the chain (the final TXT group excepted, see the recovery grammar);
  1599	   CNAME and DNAME are not followed. An empty body is `LENGTH_CAP`.
  1600	4. **Wildcards:** `INVALID / DNS_WILDCARD` (section 6.1). This is the global no-wildcard body restriction: any
  1601	   RRSIG in the body with Labels less than its owner's label count, whatever other witnesses the body carries.
  1602	   [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F07] The Labels octet is read, and this restriction applied, whenever an RRSIG's RDATA
  1603	   has at least 4 bytes (Type Covered, Algorithm, Labels), however malformed the rest of that RDATA is.
  1604	   [OWNER 2026-10-14, codified from diff-1, A07]
  1605	5. **Envelope:** ENC §6, `header ‖ u32 len ‖ body`, 1 ≤ len ≤ 2^24.
