   191	
   192	### 1.3 Serialization
   193	
   194	`canonical(v) = JCS(v)` (RFC 8785):
   195	- UTF-8 output, with no insignificant whitespace;
   196	- object members sorted by the UTF-16 code units of their names;
   197	- numbers printed by `ES`;
   198	- strings escaped only for `"`, `\` and U+0000 to U+001F: `\b \t \n \f \r` where defined, `\u00xx` with
   199	  lowercase hex otherwise. Every other scalar appears literally.
   200	
   201	*Reason: R-3.1 binds to RFC 8785. Vectors C-04 and C-05 pin the escape and the UTF-16 ordering traps, for example
   202	U+1F600 sorting before U+E000.*
   203	
   204	### 1.4 Decoding, and the order in which rejections are reported
   205	
   206	Two entry points.
   207	- `ingest(text)` takes requester JSON: whitespace is allowed, and the depth limit is 62.
   208	- `payload(bytes)` takes in-frame bytes: the depth limit is 64, and the bytes must be canonical. Before the
   209	  checks below it enforces §1.1's size limit: more than 2^24 bytes gives `LENGTH_CAP`, the code a frame's
   210	  `payload_length` check gives for the same bytes (§3.1), so the standalone entry point and the frame agree.
   211	  [OWNER 2026-10-19, P8F-04]
   212	
   213	Each runs these checks in this order and reports the **first category that fails**, scanning the whole value for
   214	each category. *Reason: both implementations then agree on the reason code, not only on rejection.*
   215	
   216	1. `JSON_ENCODING`: the bytes are not strict UTF-8. Overlongs, encoded surrogates and values above U+10FFFF are
   217	   rejected.
   218	2. `JSON_SYNTAX`:
   219	   - a BOM; not exactly one RFC 8259 JSON text; trailing non-whitespace;
   220	   - a raw control character in a string; bad escapes; leading zeros; `+`; `.5`; `1.`; `NaN`; `Infinity`.
   221	3. `JSON_DEPTH`.
   222	4. `JSON_DUPLICATE_NAME`.
   223	5. `JSON_STRING`: a surrogate, a noncharacter, an unassigned code point, or text that is not NFC.
   224	6. `JSON_NUMBER`: §1.2.
   225	7. *(`payload` only)* `JSON_NONCANONICAL`: the bytes are not equal to `JCS` of the parsed value.
   226	
