   465	## 5. Evidence: the vectors, and the two-implementation check
   466	
   467	`vectors/gen.py` is implementation A: standard library plus `rfc8785` 0.1.4 for serialization. `vectors/check.py`
   468	is implementation B: standard library only, with its own UTF-8 decoder, JSON parser, ECMAScript number formatter,
   469	JCS serializer and every decoder. Since 2026-10-12, B also has its own OpenPGP signature-packet parser and its
   470	own ECDSA P-256 verifier. The two share no code. They share only Python's Unicode 16.0.0 tables, `float`/`repr`
   471	and `hashlib`'s SHA-256.
   472	- A also uses `hmac` (RFC 6979 nonces, pinned by RFC 6979 A.2.5) and SHA-1, both only to *make* the vector
   473	  signatures.
   474	- SHA-1 fills OpenPGP's issuer-fingerprint subpacket. No check reads it, and B never computes it.
   475	
   476	| Lemma | Golden vectors | Rejection vectors |
   477	|---|---|---|
   478	| 1 (strings) | C-04, C-05, C-06 | XC-13 to XC-22, XC-28, XC-29 |
   479	| 2 (numbers) | N-01 to N-22 (RFC 8785 Appendix B), C-03, C-10, C-N01 to C-N22 | XC-03 to XC-12, XC-31 to XC-33, XF-27 |
   480	| 3 (canonical payload) | C-01 to C-09 | XC-01, XC-02, XC-23 to XC-27, XC-30, XF-23 to XF-30, XF-48 |
   481	| 4, 5 (tags, frames) | F-01 to F-03, M-01 | XF-01 to XF-22, XF-31 to XF-47, XF-49 to XF-51 |
   482	| 6 (signer frames) | F-01/F-02, R-01 | XR-01 to XR-05 |
   483	| 7 (anchor) | A-01, A-02, R-01 | XA-01 to XA-10, XA-30, XR-06 to XR-09, XR-15 |
   484	| 7a (signature slots) | SIG-01, SIG-02, A-01, A-02 | XA-11 to XA-29, XA-31, XA-32 |
   485	| (iv)(a) negative controls | R-01 | XR-10 to XR-14: a valid signature that is not the committed one fails the anchor check |
   486	| E§5.3 verification stage (P3, not P8) | R-01 | XR-16 (`SIG_INVALID`), XR-17 (`KEY_MISMATCH`) |
