   565	## 6. Limits of this evidence
   566	
   567	- The proof is prose. A reader checks it lemma by lemma, and nothing has machine-checked it. Lean was judged
   568	  unnecessary: every lemma is a decoder-inverts-encoder argument over a fixed grammar.
   569	- "Two implementations agree" is weaker than independence. Both come from one author instance on one runtime, and
   570	  they share the Unicode tables and float conversion. The V1 build is the registered second encoder (V1-DERIVATION
   571	  §5), and it must reproduce these bytes.
   572	- (N) is assumed, not tested exhaustively. N-01 to N-22 check it against RFC 8785's own Appendix B values.
   573	- The golden fingerprints (K-01 `spki-sha256`, K-02 `gpg-sha256`) use the P-256 points G and 2G, and the spec,
   574	  vector, preamble and snapshot bytes are marked ILLUSTRATIVE. The real values come from the real keys and
   575	  documents at the freeze. The layouts do not change.
   576	- The vector signatures are mathematically real, but their private keys are 1 and 2, so anyone can forge them.
   577	  They show encoding, binding and the negative control. They say nothing about unforgeability, which is (iv)(c)
   578	  and not P8 in any case.
